    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 47 tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`, including the new `Cp34Tests`.\n\n## What I did\n\nThe feature: `POST /api/owners` may include an optional `birthDate` (ISO); the response now returns an `ageBand` derived from it (`MINOR` <18, `ADULT` 18\u201364, `SENIOR` 65+), computed against the owner's `registrationDate`.\n\nSince the test creates an owner then re-fetches it, `birthDate` had to be **persisted** so `ageBand` can be recomputed on read (consistent with how the codebase derives other read-only fields in the mapper rather than storing them).\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `birthDate` (`format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` request schema and a read-only `ageBand` string to the `Owner` response schema. These drive the generated DTOs, so `OwnerFieldsDto` gains `birthDate` and `OwnerDto` gains both fields.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persisted `birthDate` `LocalDate` field (`@Column(name = \"birth_date\")`) with getter/setter. `birthDate` maps DTO\u2192entity by name through the existing generated MapStruct mapper.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"ageBand\", ...)` plus an `ageBand(owner)` default method that uses `Period.between(birthDate, registrationDate).getYears()` and buckets it, returning `null` when either date is absent (so owners without a `birthDate` map cleanly).\n\n4. **Schema files** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added a nullable `birth_date DATE` column to the `owners` table.\n\nThe active test profile (`hsqldb` + `spring-data-jpa`) persists via the JPA entity, so the entity annotation plus the schema column carry the round-trip; the openapi additions handle the request/response shape.",
